WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.760
It's about the right collaborators walking into the room together. Isn't it?

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:06.560
It is. Like opera. It's a collaborative art form.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:12.750
All these many talented craftsmen, I say talented because every profession you have to know

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:16.500
what you're doing. You have to prepare. You have to get there.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.780
But all these people that come together, the chemistry has to work.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.930
And how do you make the chemistry work?

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:26.580
Well, I'm not going to say it's a marriage or a family,

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.980
But for the moments that you're together,

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.700
it's a marriage and a family. Righ?

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.000
For those moments, you're only together for moments.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:42.840
But tolerance, give a little, all of that kind of stuff goes into movie making.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:49.150
And when it comes together, the final thing is if they don't like it, you know, move on.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:54.840
In 1977, I hate to jump around, but in 77, when.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:02.640
William Friedkin says, I want the guy, they did the Rocky movie to conduct the Academy Award show.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.330
I didn't have a clue about how to do that show.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:09.810
I had to go to Henry Mancini, Johnny Williams, Elmer Bernstein,

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:13.170
the people who had previously conducted that show.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:39.410
This whole thing is a TV show. It began in the 50s.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:42.950
There is a format for the show. Music, I'm talking about the music.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:44.750
I can only speak about music.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.760
When they say the winner is, you play the theme from the show that just won.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.520
And have been doing this since the 50s.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:59.360
I began in the 70s. 77 was the first time and I did it a number of times

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.570
Up until whatever the last time I did it... A lot of years.

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:09.040
So the melody comes in and you have to prepare for each of the five nominees in each category.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.980
Costume design, five movies, five themes. Boom, boom, boom, boom, boom.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.070
You put them on the paper for the musicians to go...

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.800
The winner is and they play the correct one.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.620
But I'm talking about the music.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.890
Over the years, you can't find a theme, for the movie.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.730
The Closer you get to this current period, you go,

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:34.290
Now the movie is from, I can't mention movies because I can't remember,

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:39.030
but there's a lot of movies with no theme. There's sound design.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:44.820
There's cans rattling. There's things that happen that go WOOSH.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:48.600
And they say, well, the winner is and you go WHOOSH.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.790
Why? Because that's the only thing they played in the movie.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:55.740
So that concept of playing the winner, has evolved or devolved,

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:00.090
into what do we do? What do we play when they win?

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:03.240
We can't find a melody and many of the scores.

